  "track": {
    "$type": "dimension",
    "$description": "tracking (letter-spacing) NAMED AS-IS -- audit P3-10. One token per distinct value the app actually renders, at exactly the value it already had, so no glyph moved. This is deliberately NOT a normalised scale: collapsing these onto two or three is a design judgement the audit parked, and this tier exists to make that judgement possible by making the set countable. MINT-ON-USE -- test/tracking_census.py FAILS on a token nothing uses, which is the property --space-19/39/43 never had. The em tokens must stay @property-UNREGISTERED: a registered <length> computes at :root and every uppercase label would stop tracking its own type size.",
    "none": {
      "$value": "0",
      "$description": "an explicit reset of inherited tracking (.mhp-sub inside a .mhp-h that tracks 0.5px), not an absent declaration"
    },
